13. Why G1 can scale better than a naive full-heap collector

        Imagine a 32 GB heap.
        
        A naive approach could be:
                                    Stop application
                                            ↓
                                    Scan huge heap
                                            ↓
                                    Find garbage
                                            ↓
                                    Compact everything
                                            ↓
                                    Resume application

That can create unacceptable pause times.

G1 instead thinks more incrementally:
                                        Heap
                                         ↓
                                        Regions
                                         ↓
                                        Collect selected regions
                                         ↓
                                        Evacuate live objects
                                         ↓
                                        Reclaim regions
                                         ↓
                                        Continue application

And separately, G1 performs concurrent marking work to understand the state of the old generation.

That is the fundamental architectural idea.
===============================================================================================================================================
14. Where does Collection Set fit?

        During a GC pause, G1 builds a Collection Set, commonly abbreviated CSet.
        
        Think:
                Heap regions
                
                R1  Eden      ← selected
                R2  Eden      ← selected
                R3  Old       ← selected
                R4  Old
                R5  Survivor
                R6  Old
                R7  Free

The selected regions form the collection set: CSet = {R1, R2, R3}
G1 then performs evacuation for those regions.

For a Young GC, the collection set is primarily young regions.
For a Mixed GC, it can include:
                                Young regions
                                       +
                                selected Old regions
That's an important bridge to your next topic.
===============================================================================================================================================
15. Young GC vs Mixed GC

            Young GC:                        
                        Conceptually:
                                        Eden + Survivor
                                               ↓
                                         evacuation
                                               ↓
                                        Survivor / Old


            Mixed GC:
                    Conceptually:
                                    Young regions
                                          +
                                    selected Old regions
                                          ↓
                                        evacuation
                                          ↓
                                    Survivor / Old / Free

            Why does G1 collect Old regions?            
                Because eventually the application accumulates long-lived objects.            
                G1's concurrent marking determines information about old-region liveness.            
                Then G1 can choose old regions that are worthwhile to reclaim.
            
            That's where the name Garbage-First becomes meaningful.
===============================================================================================================================================
16. What exactly does "Garbage-First" mean?

        A common oversimplification is:        
                    "G1 sorts regions by percentage of garbage."
        
        That's not a precise description.

        A better L6 explanation is:

                G1 uses internal heuristics and cost predictions to select regions whose 
                reclamation provides useful memory recovery within its pause-time objectives.

        So the collector considers both:
        
                    Potential reclaim
                            +
                    Estimated evacuation/processing cost
                            +
                    Pause-time goal
        
        This is a much more architecturally accurate explanation.
