17. Spring Boot production example

Imagine your service has:
                         Kubernetes Pod
                              │
                              ▼
                        Spring Boot
                              │
                              ▼
                        OrderController
                              │
                              ▼
                        OrderService
                              │
                              ▼
                        OrderRepository
                              │
                              ▼
                        PostgreSQL

Suppose the service processes:
                10,000 requests/sec

Every request creates temporary objects.

Therefore:
            High request rate
                   ↓
            High allocation rate
                   ↓
            Eden fills quickly
                   ↓
            Young GC frequency increases

If GC cannot keep up:
                        Allocation rate
                               >
                        Reclamation capability

eventually memory pressure increases.
This is why allocation rate is one of the most important GC performance metrics.

