19. What should you say if the interviewer asks: "Is G1 concurrent?"

        The best answer:
        
        "Partially. G1 combines Stop-The-World phases, such as evacuation pauses, 
        with concurrent phases such as marking. So I would not describe G1 as a 
        completely concurrent collector. Its design goal is to perform enough work concurrently 
        and incrementally to reduce the duration and frequency of disruptive pauses."
        
        That is an excellent L6-level answer.

